2026-10-07  Mario Maia  <mario.mtbr+github@outlook.com>

	* apt-blacklist: Created apt-blacklist, file dedicated to
	blacklist APT packages. It's best to keep it short and blacklist
	only trully problematic packages. Note that coreutils-from-uutils
	is blacklisted in another file.

	* bash_aliases: Created the file, with aliases for backing up and
	restoring gpg keys.

	* fortune: Created a dedicated folder for fortune files, named
	"fortunes". This will make it easier to have multiple fortune
	files and to configure auto-compilation of such files.

	* fortunes/bible: File has been created.

	* Makefile (BUILD_ESSENTIAL): The package build-essential is no
	longer installed; instead, its dependencies are installed
	explicitly. This is because Ubuntu is forcing the adoption of
	coreutils-from-uutils, a Rust-based implementation of coreutils,
	by having coreutils-from-uutils as a dependency of build-essential
	and not having coreutils-from-gnu as an alternative dependency.

2026-08-31  Mario Maia  <mario.mtbr+github@outlook.com>

	* fortunes: A fortune file has been created and is already in use
	by Bash and Emacs. Pertinent targets have also been implemented in
	the Makefile.

	* init.el (:changelog): Emacs changelog functionality has been
	configured (basically, the name and email variables have been
	set). Also, a ChangeLog file (this one, in fact) for this
	repository has been created.
